From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 00:52:33 -0400
Subject: add the Clear row above the new-tab row

The reference has a hairline above the new-tab row with a Clear at its trailing
end, which empties the Space you are looking at. Clear closes that Space's tabs
and leaves the pinned ones -- the essentials, which belong to every Space --
where they are.

Tabs are collected before any are closed, because closing shifts every index
behind it.

Two Views notes, both found the slow way. views::Separator paints its whole
bounds whatever preferred size it is given, so the hairline is a plain view with
a background. And FlexLayout stretched that view to the row's height whatever
cross-axis alignment it was told, on the layout or on the child; BoxLayout
honours the alignment, so the row uses that.

Why: it was the last thing in docs/UI-SPEC.md's sidebar that had nothing built
for it.
Removable when: never, short of dropping Spaces.
